ares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & {5}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0f92926-0c15-554a-8fba-55b05d435980" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Least-Squares Regression Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5ec7832-8932-58c5-b893-30f453051610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(XX^{T})^{-1}Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132386} {:answer/id #uuid "b2561912-2be6-5752-8830-9949288ed927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X(X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132387} {:answer/id #uuid "c701b87a-8b7e-5dab-8360-8da180243ca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X^{T}(XX^{T})^{-1}Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132388} {:answer/id #uuid "e8bc1d73-c12e-5285-9cd0-fa7c532775e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132389} {:answer/id #uuid "0e55c8e4-aa7a-52cf-b503-a16cb0bc47c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X^{T}(XX^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132390}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6fda705d-d1bb-56ec-97e8-e3c1b26c78ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132385}] :question/id #uuid "ecf29c4b-376c-5cb9-b877-1eb8940529e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42409" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x + β_{2}x^{2}$ that best fits the data.\n\n$X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & 5^{2}\\end{bmatrix}, β = \\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2}\\end{bmatrix}, y = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}]}
